## MCP Server Integration

Both SDKs use the same conceptual model: HTTP transport (with static `headers` or OAuth `auth`) or stdio (with `command` / `args` / `env`). Pass servers inline on `Agent.create` or `agent.send` for the most common case.

| Runtime | Transport | Details |
|---|---|---|
| **Local agents** | stdio or HTTP | stdio servers available on caller's machine; OAuth login can reuse Cursor's saved login but can't open browser to sign in |
| **Cloud agents** | HTTP or stdio | HTTP servers; stdio runs inside the cloud VM. HTTP `headers` and `auth` handled by Cursor's backend and redacted before the VM sees them. Stdio `env` values passed into the VM -- treat like runtime secrets. |

**Critical**: Inline servers fully replace creation-time servers on a per-send override -- not merged. If you resume an agent and still need MCP tools, pass servers again on the resume call. Inline servers are not persisted.

